{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22598 - PROTEIN:6075",
  "verbalization": "Crassocolide F is implicated in the regulation of Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2 through multiple pathways, with the target entity EDD domain protein, DegV family acting as a common intermediate. The evidence suggests that Crassocolide F interacts with this protein, which is subsequently targeted by various compounds, including 6(2H)-Benzofuranone and (3R,4aR,8aR)-8a-methyl-5-methylidene-3-prop-1-en-2-yl-1,2,3,4,4a,6,7,8-octahydronaphthalene, all of which are linked to the endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2. This indicates a potential mechanism involving the inhibition of the enzyme, possibly through direct binding or allosteric modulation. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same enzyme suggests a possible role in the regulation of protein degradation or processing in the endoplasmic reticulum. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Crassocolide F and the enzyme, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
